cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "A calibrated regional screening framework for SPT N-values from public borehole records under strict spatial cross-validation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Okauchi"
    given-names: "Ryota"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-5391-7133"
    affiliation: "The University of Tokyo"
    website: "https://github.com/R-Okauchi"
  - family-names: "Chun"
    given-names: "Pang-jo"
    affiliation: "The University of Tokyo"
abstract: >-
  A calibrated regional screening framework that turns the public
  KuniJiban borehole archive into a pre-investigation predictive
  product over raw SPT N-values, evaluated under a mesh-keyed
  spatial K-fold protocol on 495,725 measurements from 21,031
  unique boreholes over the Japanese Kanto plain. The framework
  treats the regressor as a configurable component and instantiates
  it with six interchangeable candidates (DKL+SVGP, CatBoost,
  LightGBM, XGBoost, LightGBM-CQR, GPBoost). Under proper spatial
  K-fold, no single regressor dominates: CatBoost wins random-fold
  point estimate, GPBoost wins contiguous-fold point estimate by a
  substantial margin (paired BCa 95% CI excludes zero), and
  LightGBM-CQR wins random-fold stiff-layer conformal coverage. A
  model-agnostic split-conformal layer with a Mondrian (regime by
  depth) conditional-coverage decomposition substantially reduces
  the marginal coverage deficit, reaching near-nominal coverage
  under random mesh folds while exposing residual under-coverage
  under contiguous spatial extrapolation. A right-censored survival
  reformulation of the depth-to-first-stiff endpoint incorporates
  the 65.2% of boreholes that did not encounter N >= 30 within
  their surveyed depth; the released survival predictor is Random
  Survival Forest because the Schoenfeld test rejects the Cox
  proportional-hazards assumption at p < 10^-12 across all spatial
  folds. Engineering-facing primitives accompany the release
  (isotonic-recalibrated threshold classifiers, per-borehole
  soft-layer and upper-10 m regressors, and a do-not-trust mask
  for locations more than 5 km from any training borehole).
keywords:
